  "_comment": "MBTA V3 predictions (https://api-v3.mbta.com/predictions) fixtures for qa/boston-dogfood-gate.mjs's live-predictions pass (docs/jim-brief-boston-subway-live-predictions.md, 20 Sep 2026). Each of `harvard`/`kenmoreGreenTrunk`/`southStation` is one {data, included} payload shaped exactly like a real filter[stop]=<...>&filter[route_type]=0,1,2&include=trip,route response, injected into the REAL fetchStationBoard() via its `rawPredictions` option, so the production drop/map/sort pipeline (mapPredictionToTrip in lib/providers/boston.js) is what runs here, not a copy of it. Rows marked \"_source\": \"live-capture-20260920\" are REAL, unedited MBTA V3 responses (one call each to Harvard place-harsq, Kenmore place-kencl, and South Station place-sstat plus its Commuter Rail platform ids, sequential, well under the ~20/min unauthenticated rate limit) trimmed to a representative subset: `harvard` is subway-only (Red Line) and includes one real CANCELLED row (departure_time null) and one real row carrying a live `status` string (\"Stopped 3 stops away\"); `kenmoreGreenTrunk` is a Green Line C/D trunk station and includes one real arrival-only row (schedule_relationship ADDED, departure_time null, arrival_time set — a mid-trip train reported as terminating here) alongside real Cleveland Circle (Green-C) and Riverside (Green-D) departures; `southStation` is the subway+Commuter-Rail dual-mode station and includes real Red Line rows plus real CR-Providence/CR-Franklin/CR-Fairmount rows (including one real arrival-only CR-Worcester row and real \"All aboard\"/\"Now boarding\"/\"Stopped N stops away\" status strings) — note CR-Providence and CR-Franklin share one real trip id here (SavinHillWestRoxbury-860989-5821), a genuine MBTA quirk for a combined train that later splits, not a fixture error. Rows marked \"_source\": \"synthetic\" (harvard's SKIPPED and NON_REVENUE rows) are hand-authored — neither happened to be running at capture time — so both drop paths named in the brief are covered without waiting for one to occur live.",
